Hello HMECOLOGY members

A reminder - Ecological data often contain observations grouped within sites or other sampling units. Multilevel/Mixed Models Using Stata is a 2-day seminar livestreaming November 17 and 20 with Meghan Cain (StataCorp). Multilevel models in Stata can represent ecological observations nested within sampling units. Random-intercept and random-slope models provide ways to examine variation across those units. The material also covers mixed models for count responses and methods for comparing models.

Details and registration: https://instats.org/seminar/multilevelmixed-models-using-stata
Further information is available on the seminar page.

Best wishes

